.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt WC 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm wc
.Nd count newlines, words and bytes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l
.Op Fl w
.Op Fl c
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Read each file, or standard input when there are no operands.
Print newline, word and byte counts in that order.
Words are runs of bytes other than ASCII whitespace; this is not a Unicode
word or character count.
An unterminated final line does not add a newline count.
.Pp
.Fl l ,
.Fl w
and
.Fl c
select only the requested counts and may be combined, as
.Fl lwc .
Leading dash words are options; there is no
.Ql --
terminator.
Use
.Ql ./-name
for a dash-leading path.
An explicit
.Ql -
is a path, not standard input.
.Pp
Output columns align to the widest count and named-file rows include the
path.
Multiple file operands add a total row for successfully read files.
A failed read is diagnosed on standard error and later files are attempted.
Files are only read through the process's filesystem view.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when all inputs were read; 1 for a read/open failure;
2 for an unknown option letter.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wc -l /var/log/sshd
cat /etc/network.conf | wc -c
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cat 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
